UID:stichting-stokroos-residency-fundaziun-nairs-2026@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T092459Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260911
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260912
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Stokroos: Residency at Fundaziun Nairs 2026
DESCRIPTION:Stichting Stokroos funds a three-month reflective residency at 
 Fundaziun Nairs in Scuol\, Switzerland\, for one selected visual artist\, 
 designer or craft practitioner (overlap possible). Both emerging and estab
 lished makers may apply. Stokroos covers full accommodation and meals dire
 ctly with Fundaziun Nairs and provides a discretionary EUR 7\,000 budget f
 or living\, travel and production. The application should include a propos
 al that engages specifically with the residency\, its Alpine surroundings 
 and/or its historical and cultural context. Eligibility: you completed you
 r first subject-specific (vocational or higher) programme in 2022 or earli
 er\, or have an equivalent established practice\, or started without forma
 l training (first presentation marks the start of your practice)\; at leas
 t 21 years old\; living and working in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (inc
 luding its Caribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; not curren
 tly enrolled in a study or post-academic programme. Applications are indiv
 idual only\; duos and collectives cannot apply. Makers already selected by
  Fundaziun Nairs may still apply if they meet the criteria. You may submit
  only one application per year across all Stokroos grants\, and must not h
 ave received a Seed Grant rejection in the previous calendar year. Apply v
 ia the online form (Dutch or English) with a portfolio PDF up to 20 pages\
 , optional video up to 10 minutes total\, CV up to 2 pages\, and work/plan
  descriptions up to 2\,500 characters each. Selection includes an introduc
 tory interview with up to three candidates\; Stokroos aims to respond with
 in 8 weeks. No appeal is possible. Application window: 1 to 11 September 2
 026. More information at nairs.ch.\n\nOrganisation: Stichting Stokroos\nLo
 cation: Residency in Scuol\, Switzerland (Fundaziun Nairs). Applicants mus
 t live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean
  parts) or Suriname for at least one year. Applicants outside the Randstad
  particularly encouraged.\nAward: Fully supported stay (accommodation and 
 meals paid directly to Fundaziun Nairs) plus an unrestricted living\, trav
 el and production budget of EUR 7\,000. 80% paid before the residency\, th
 e remainder on receipt of a brief final report. No application fee.\nDurat
 ion: Intensive three-month working period (July through September).\n\nMor
 e: https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/guidelines-residency-fundaziun-nairs
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/guidelines-residency-fundaziun-nairs
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency in Scuol\, Switzerland (Fundaziun Nairs). Applicants mus
 t live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean
  parts) or Suriname for at least one year. Applicants outside the Randstad
  particularly encouraged.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eofa-artistic-research-residency-geneva-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261102T092459Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Embassy of Foreign Artists: Artistic Research Residency i
 n International Organisation Archives (Geneva\, 2027)
DESCRIPTION:The Embassy of Foreign Artists\, in partnership with the Centre
  for Digital Humanities and Multilateralism at the Geneva Graduate Institu
 te\, invites artists worldwide to a three-month artistic research residenc
 y in Geneva during 2027. The programme centres on archival research in the
  archives of Geneva-based international intergovernmental and non-governme
 ntal organisations (UN\, Red Cross and others): uncovering untold stories\
 , examining international decision-making\, reflecting on multilateral suc
 cesses and failures\, and imagining new possibilities for international co
 operation. Selected artists receive a CHF 1\,400 monthly residency grant\,
  accommodation in a private room with shared common areas\, artistic guida
 nce from EOFA\, connections with archive personnel\, and access to partici
 pating archives as primary research resource\; travel and production costs
  are the artist's own. ELIGIBILITY: professional artistic practice with a 
 demonstrable body of work (creations\, publications and/or performances)\,
  over 28 years old\, fluent in French or English\, not enrolled in basic a
 rt training\; individuals\, duos or groups may apply (same stipend). APPLY
  via the online form plus a single PDF (cover letter\, project description
 \, portfolio\, CV) emailed to application@eofa.ch. No application fee. Dea
 dline: 15 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Embassy of Foreign Artists / Ce
 ntre for Digital Humanities and Multilateralism\, Geneva Graduate Institut
 e\nLocation: Geneva\, Switzerland\nAward: CHF 1\,400 monthly residency gra
 nt plus accommodation in a private room\; travel and artistic production c
 osts are not covered\nDuration: 3 months\, during 2027\n\nMore: https://ww
 w.eofa.ch/en/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.eofa.ch/en/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Geneva\, Switzerland
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:schlossmediale-werdenberg-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T092459Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:Deadline: Schlossmediale Call for Art Residency 2027 (Schloss Werde
 nberg\, Switzerland)
DESCRIPTION:Schlossmediale\, the international festival of early music\, ne
 w music and audiovisual art at Werdenberg Castle in the canton of St. Gall
 en\, invites three solo artists to a five-week residency from 17 May to 27
  June 2027. The works developed on site are shown in the castle during the
  14th festival edition (17-26 June 2027). The 2027 theme is KLATSCH! (Rumo
 ur-Impact): sound and rumour\, applause and gossip\, oral tradition\, coll
 ective memory\, and the ways every era spreads its information. MEDIUMS: s
 ound art\, sound studies\, audiovisual art\, experimental instrument build
 ing\, visual art\, installation\, sculpture\, land art and performance\; s
 ound installations without a visual dimension are not considered. SUPPORT:
  CHF 4\,000 grant\, CHF 1\,000 for travel\, transport and meals\, up to CH
 F 1\,000 for materials\, and accommodation in a shared house in Werdenberg
  (individual rooms\, shared kitchen and living areas). ELIGIBILITY: solo a
 rtists with professional experience (no groups or duos) who can live and w
 ork on site for the full period and complete a finished\, functional work 
 by the festival opening\; residents present their work on castle tours and
  attend the whole festival. Working space at the castle is limited and no 
 studios are provided. HOW TO APPLY: exclusively online via the application
  portal linked from the open-call page. DEADLINE: 18 October 2026.\n\nOrga
 nisation: Schlossmediale Werdenberg\nLocation: Werdenberg Castle\, canton 
 of St. Gallen\, Switzerland. Open internationally to solo artists\; accomm
 odation in a shared house in Werdenberg.\nAward: CHF 4\,000 grant per resi
 dent\, plus CHF 1\,000 for travel\, transport and meals\, up to CHF 1\,000
  for material costs\, and accommodation in a shared house (individual room
 s). Three residencies awarded.\nDuration: Five-week residency from 17 May 
 to 27 June 2027\, with the 14th Schlossmediale festival on 17-26 June 2027
 \n\nMore: https://schlossmediale.ch/festival-schlossmediale/ausstellung/op
 en-call-2027-en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://schlossmediale.ch/festival-schlossmediale/ausstellung/open-call
 -2027-en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Werdenberg Castle\, canton of St. Gallen\, Switzerland. Open inter
 nationally to solo artists\; accommodation in a shared house in Werdenberg
 .
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:traces-art-science-energypolis-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261102T092459Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: TRACES Art & Science @ Energypolis 2027: residency at the
  EPFL Laboratory for Energy Materials (Sion)
DESCRIPTION:TRACES is a new art and science residency run by the Foundation
  for the Sustainable Development of Mountain Regions (FDDM) with EPFL Vala
 is-Wallis\, Energypolis\, the City of Sion and the Canton of Valais. The 2
 027 pilot embeds one visual artist for three months in Prof. Sascha Feldma
 nn's Laboratory for Energy Materials at EPFL\, which works on light-matter
  interactions and soft semiconductors for flexible solar cells\, energy-ef
 ficient screens and emerging quantum technologies. The artist develops ori
 ginal work in dialogue with the lab around the energy transition and the m
 aterials of the future\, with studio and production space\, scientific men
 toring and a public final presentation on 15 April 2027. ELIGIBILITY: conf
 irmed\, professional international visual artists aged 25 or over who fini
 shed their studies at least two years ago and have at least two years of p
 rofessional practice\; applications in English or French with a letter of 
 intent (two A4 pages)\, portfolio and CV via the online form. Laureate sel
 ected 7 December 2026. DEADLINE: 22 November 2026\, 23:59 Swiss time (CET)
 .\n\nOrganisation: Foundation for the Sustainable Development of Mountain 
 Regions (FDDM) with EPFL Valais-Wallis\nLocation: Energypolis campus\, Sio
 n\, Valais\, Switzerland. In person.\nAward: Artist stipend of CHF 2\,000 
 per month (CHF 6\,000 total) covering living and research costs\, housing 
 in Sion\, travel from home and back up to CHF 1\,500\, and a separate prod
 uction budget set by the curator. No application fee.\nDuration: Three mon
 ths\, 11 January to 18 April 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.traces-opencall.ch
 /en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.traces-opencall.ch/en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Energypolis campus\, Sion\, Valais\, Switzerland. In person.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
